# Deployment bundles created for uploading plugin folders to the server.
# These are packaging artifacts, not source: the PHP under src/moodle is the
# source of truth and the tarballs are rebuilt on demand.
*.tar

# Pre-generated Computing narration. One clip per Listen button, named by a hash
# of the button's text, so a rebuilt script mints a new file rather than
# changing an existing one — committing them would grow the pack by the full
# size of the audio on every narration pass and never shrink it again. The
# clips are a deploy artifact: tools/generate-ehel-computing-audio.js makes them
# and tools/upload-media-to-bunny.js computing ships them to the CDN.
#
# Scoped to Computing. Science still tracks its clips and that is its session's
# call to change.
src/prototypes/ehel-academy/computing/media/audio/tts/

# Mathematics narration, ignored for the same reason. This tree had already
# accumulated 4,346 unreachable clips (1.73 GB) before anyone noticed: a clip is
# named by a hash of its Listen button's text, so every wording fix silently
# strands the previous file rather than replacing it. Committing them meant the
# pack grew by the full size of the audio on each pass and never shrank.
#
# tools/generate-ehel-math-audio.js makes them and
# tools/upload-media-to-bunny.js mathematics ships them to
# media/mathematics/gNN/audio/tts/, the path course-ui.js builds off localhost.
src/prototypes/ehel-academy/mathematics/media/audio/tts/

# Intensive English narration is TRACKED, unlike Computing's and Mathematics'
# above. It was ignored here from 2026-08-02 (345966ad4) for their reason, and
# the rule was removed on 2026-08-24 because it never delivered it.
#
# That commit ignored the clips on the stated basis that they "were untracked
# and undecided: 5,275 files, 507 MB". They were not: 4,752 of them had been
# committed the day before, in 54ca560d5. gitignore does not retroactively
# untrack, so the rule only ever hid the ~500 not yet added plus everything
# generated afterwards — 848 files by 2026-08-24. The saving it was written for
# was already spent: 439.8 MB sat in history regardless, and removing the rule
# costs 163.9 MB on top of it rather than the 507 MB the comment implied.
#
# So the choice was consistency in one direction or the other, and this subject
# now matches Science, Global Perspectives and English, which all commit their
# clips. Untracking the 4,744 instead would not shrink history by a byte — the
# blobs stay — so it would have bought only a stop to future growth, at the cost
# of leaving the one subject with two copies down to one.
#
# The growth argument itself is real and still applies: a clip is named by a
# hash of its Listen button's text, so every wording fix strands the previous
# file rather than replacing it. Run tools/prune-ehel-course-audio.mjs
# intensive-english after any content change; now that git holds the clips it
# will delete orphans without --force, which is the thing tracking buys.

# Rendered marketing video. The 15 MB infomercial is a build of
# docs/marketing/ehel-academy-infomercial.html and its script, both of which are
# tracked — the render is reproducible from them, and every re-render would add
# its full size to history permanently rather than replacing the last one.
# Distribute the finished video from the CDN, not from a clone.
docs/marketing/*.mp4

# Claude Code session worktrees (git worktree add under .claude/worktrees/).
# Nested inside the repo, so without this a whole-tree `git add` stages one as an
# embedded repository. Several sessions share this checkout - see CLAUDE.md :: Git.
.claude/worktrees/
